# VESPER HALL 1F -- grand foyer, dining hall (W), the late Lord's study (E)
# Tileset: TILESET_MANSION (Celadon Mansion). 15x8 blocks, buffer 294/1300.
# Front door (doormat, bottom centre) faces the estate grounds. Two grand
# staircases (block 06) flank the north door (17) to the Portrait Gallery.
# Dining hall: pink carpet room behind a 0a/0b/0c partition, banquet table
# (10 x2) with chairs (1b); doorway at its bottom-right (0c).
# Study: behind a 20 partition with a gap at row 4. The cellar stair (15, x12)
# is HIDDEN: ship the map with 18 (bookshelf) there and `changeblock 24, 0, $15`
# once the Head Butler hands over the CELLAR KEY (after the 2F burglars).
# Portrait plaques (09) either side of the north door: the Vesper family.
# Gap: no grand two-flight staircase or fireplace in the tileset; the twin 06
# stairs either side of the door stand in for a split staircase.
ref CeladonMansion1F
tileset mansion
key X=00 ,=02 .=03 W=04 <=05 >=06 w=07 v=08 p=09 r=0a |=0b c=0c T=0d M=0e B=0f O=10 P=11 k=12 S=15 s=16 D=17 K=18 h=1b C=1c !=20
grid:
PkPrW>pDp>!BSKP
,,,|......!....
hOh|..,,,.!..O.
hOh|..,,,.!....
,,,c..,,,......
vvvv......!....
..........!vvvv
.......M.......
end
exit FRONT 14 15
exit FRONT2 15 15
exit GALLERY 15 0
exit STAIR_W 11 0
exit STAIR_E 19 0
exit CELLAR 24 0
obj npc 15 3 HeadButler down
obj trainer 6 4 MaidRosa down 3
obj trainer 24 9 ButlerHugo left 4
obj sign 13 0 PortraitLord
obj sign 17 0 PortraitLady
obj sign 26 5 LordsDesk
obj item 1 13 ElixirSW
obj hidden 0 2 DiningShelf
